A||N||5||dgroves||Quick recovery valve||||5||
Z||000000||dgroves||08-13-2001||11:10 AM||||Does anybody know how to check the quick recovery valve in the master cylinder. Should it be one way  or is it just a metering orifice that should flow both ways?<P>My back brakes don't seem to work much at all. The front calipers don't return and the pads drag. The rotors,wheels, etc. get real hot. ||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||08-13-2001||07:22 PM||||sounds like multiple problems.<P>MC hangup could be the MC itself or the brake booster isn't right. try backing off the MC anchor nuts on the booster a couple turns and see if the front brakes let go. <P>QT valve in MC flows fluid both directions but the flow is regulated. QT valve usually won't bother the front brakes.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 08-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||dgroves||08-15-2001||01:26 PM||||Ogre, Thanks for the reply. I went ahead and replaced the MC and bled everything. That cured the problem of the calipers not retracting. I had also replaced the vacum booster but the brakes require LOTS of pedal pressure to work. Is there a test that I can do to tell if I got a defective vacum booster?||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||08-15-2001||08:12 PM||||The replacement booster may be bad.<P>Is the effort about the same with the motor running and stopped?<P>Check the check valve... it's that odd plastic elbow where the line connects to the booster. that could be bad.<P>If it's got a filter in the vac line, check that over. it could be damaged or full of crap. That's back in the engine bay. just follow the line.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Max The Chainsaw||08-15-2001||09:11 PM||||Well, the "normal" way to test a vacuum booster is to hold the pedal down and start the car. If the booster works, the pedal should drop slightly when the engine vacuum hits it.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||dgroves||08-16-2001||02:00 PM||||OK Guys,<BR>I checked the vacum at the manifold and at the booster. It's 15 1n hg at both spots. That would eliminate the filter. Just to double check, I took the filter out of the line and drove the car. Couldn't tell any difference. Did the "Pedal drop" test that Chainsaw suggested and the pedal didn't move when the engine vacum came on. Very little if any difference in pedal feel with engine on or off. Kinda looks like I got a defective part. Thanks guys! ||||reg||1
